.TH AUTHORIZED_KEYS 5
.SH NAME
authorized_keys, known_hosts, sshd_config \- the SSH files
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
.br
.B ~/.ssh/known_hosts
.br
.BR ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 ", " ~/.ssh/id_ed25519.pub
.br
.B /etc/ssh/sshd_config
.br
.BR /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key ", " .pub
.SH DESCRIPTION
SIEOS's SSH uses OpenSSH's file formats, Ed25519 keys only.
.TP
.B ~/.ssh/authorized_keys
the keys
.BR sshd (8)
lets in as this user: "ssh-ed25519 KEY comment" lines.
Options before the key are skipped, not applied.
A locked encrypted home cannot be read, so its keys count only while it is
open (the user logged in elsewhere); a password works always.
.TP
.B ~/.ssh/known_hosts
the servers
.BR ssh (1)
has seen: "host" (port 22) or "[host]:port", then the key.
A first connection asks, and yes adds the line; a host whose key changed is
refused, with its new fingerprint and the line to remove.
.TP
.BR ~/.ssh/id_ed25519 ", " id_ed25519.pub
the user's key, made by
.BR ssh-keygen (1):
OpenSSH's private key format, unencrypted (a key with a passphrase is
reported and skipped), and its public line.
.TP
.B /etc/ssh/sshd_config
the switch: sshd starts at boot only if this file exists. Nothing in it is
read yet.
.TP
.BR /etc/ssh/ssh_host_ed25519_key ", " .pub
the server's host key, made on its first start (mode 0600, root only).
.SH EXAMPLES
To turn the server on (as root):
.nf
mkdir /etc/ssh
echo on > /etc/ssh/sshd_config
svc restart sshd
.fi
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR ssh (1),
.BR ssh-keygen (1),
.BR sshd (8)
